    "messages": [
      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": "Make a video explaining how password reset works in our web app: the user says they forgot their password, the app looks up their account, emails them a one-time link, and the user opens it and chooses a new password."
      },
      {
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "I've drafted the graph. It has five parts: the user, the web app, the users database, and the email service, with the app and database grouped as your backend. The flow runs from the forgotten-password request, to the account lookup, to the emailed link, to the new password, which the app saves and uses to sign the user in.\n\nAssumptions I made:\n- The web app and user database are run by your team.\n- The email service is a third party.\n- The link is one-time, but the video won't show its expiry.\n- The user is signed in right after setting the new password.\n\nIs the graph right? If so, I'll move on to agreeing the story with you.",
        "toolCalls": []
      },
      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": "The graph looks good. I approve it."
      },
      {
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "Graph approved. Next is the story. Here's what I suggest:\n\n- **Who it's for:** people who use the app, not its developers.\n- **The one thing to remember:** a reset link works once, and only for an hour.\n- **Shape:** problem, how it works, outcome. It opens on the forgotten password and ends with the user signed in with a new password.\n- **Hook:** \"Someone can't remember their password.\"\n\nDoes this story work? Tell me if you'd like a different audience, takeaway or hook, or anything to stress or leave out. Once you approve it, I'll save it and draft the script.",
        "toolCalls": []
      },
      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": "Yes, that story works for me. Go ahead and write the script."
      },
      {
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "The script is drafted: one scene with nine beats, about 47 seconds long. It opens on \"Someone can't remember their password,\" follows the reset request, the account lookup, the emailed one-time link, and the new password, and ends with the user signed in. The first beat's line was too long for the hook, so I shortened it.\n\nI also assumed the reset link goes to the email address on the account, and that the link expires after one use or one hour, whichever comes first.\n\nIs the script right? If so, I'll offer a title card: \"Password reset, step by step\", with \"A reset link works once, and only for an hour.\" underneath.",
        "toolCalls": []
      },
      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": "The script looks good. I approve it."
      },
